 # Hyperprior for Entropy Estimation
 
-Also called: Factorized Hyperprior for $\hat{z}$
 
 ## Overview
-The hyperprior method uses a latent variable $\hat{z}$ to model dependencies for Gaussian probability estimation during entropy coding, following Ballé et al. (2018). It sets apart from sibling context models by providing a global or local statistical prior for the quantized attributes $\hat{y}$, whereas context models rely on neighboring spatial or structural relationships. In 3D Gaussian Splatting (3DGS) compression, this method contributes less to compression performance than inter- and intra-context models because 3DGS attributes exhibit less intra-Gaussian redundancy compared to image pixels [S1, unofficial].
