 ## Background
-The hyperprior approach originates from Ballé et al. (2018), originally designed for image compression. It was adapted for 3D Gaussian Splatting compression in the FCGS model (Fast Feedforward 3D Gaussian Splatting Compression) [S1, unofficial]. The method leverages information theory principles where bit consumption is calculated based on the negative log-likelihood of the estimated probability distributions [S1, unofficial].
